{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Human-Centered AI.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Human-Centered AI.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"human centered ai human centered ai","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Human-Centered AI.md","fileName":"Human-Centered AI.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Human-Centered AI","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Governance and Responsible Innovation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Governance and Responsible Innovation","Anthropocentrism in AI Ethics","Sustainable AI","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Human-Centered AI.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Human-Centered AI.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"human centered ai human centered ai","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Human-Centered AI.md","fileName":"Human-Centered AI.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Human-Centered AI","heading":"Human-Centered AI","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Human-centered AI directs the design and governance of artificial intelligence toward human dignity, agency, rights, and well-being. It rejects systems that make people serve technical optimization and requires that important automated processes remain answerable to those they affect.\n\nThe approach is valuable when it protects people from manipulation or unaccountable power, but its scope is contested. A strictly human-centric policy can neglect animals, ecosystems, and the material conditions on which human life depends. [[Anthropocentrism in AI Ethics]] identifies this limit, while [[Sustainable AI]] expands the account of responsible design beyond immediate human users.","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Governance and Responsible Innovation","Anthropocentrism in AI Ethics","Sustainable AI","aiethics.epub"],"pro